      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the prospective use of an electrocardiographic sign--lead aVR ST-segment elevation greater than that seen in lead V(1)--in patients with an acute coronary syndrome as a method to prompt early angiography, to withhold clopidogrel therapy, and to perform urgent coronary bypass surgery leading to successful clinical outcomes."},
